.\" No version in the title line: see the note in irontile.1.
.TH IRONTILE-POLKIT 1 "" "irontile" "irontile"
.SH NAME
irontile\-polkit \- the authentication agent irontile's session registers with polkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B irontile\-polkit
.br
.B irontile\-polkit \-\-dump
.I PATH
.br
.B irontile\-polkit \-\-try
.SH DESCRIPTION
polkit decides whether something may be done; an agent is what asks the person
at the keyboard.
.B irontile\-polkit
registers as that agent for the session. Without one, every action that needs
an administrator fails with nobody to ask \(em which from the chair looks like a
button that does nothing.
.PP
Start it with the session and leave it running: an agent that exits is an agent
that unregisters.
.PP
.EX
[startup]
exec = [
  "irontile\-polkit",
]
.EE
.PP
Only one agent can hold a session. A desktop that ships its own will take the
registration if it starts first, and whichever loses is a silent no\-op.
.B pkttyagent \-\-fallback,
which
.BR pkexec (1)
starts for itself in a terminal, registers for one process rather than for the
session and does not collide.
.PP
Nothing here is privileged. The password goes to
.BR polkit\-agent\-helper\-1 ,
the setuid helper polkit ships for exactly this, which does the checking and
tells the authority; the agent learns whether the answer was accepted and
nothing else. Three attempts are offered, as sudo allows, and a refusal redraws
the dialog rather than closing it.
.PP
With no compositor to draw on it asks on the terminal instead. That is not a
nicety: an agent that can only ask through a window is an agent that cannot be
used to fix a broken window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-dump " PATH"
Render the dialog to a PNG and exit, without waiting for anything to ask. A
prompt that only appears when something wants an administrator is a prompt
nobody can look at.
.TP
.B \-\-try
Show the dialog with a made\-up request and print how long the answer was. For
looking at it on a real display without waiting for something to want an
administrator.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a usage message and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR irontile (1),
.BR polkit (8),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR pkttyagent (1)
